  "verbalization": "Duloxetine, a serotonin-norepinephrine reuptake inhibitor (SNRI), is linked to Major Depressive Disorder (MDD) through a chain of indications that involve anxiety disorders. The evidence suggests that Duloxetine may be repurposed for MDD due to its indirect pathway through anxiety-related conditions. Specifically, Duloxetine is indicated for Anxiety Disorder, which in turn is linked to Vortioxetine and Desvenlafaxine, both of which are indicated for MDD. This suggests a potential mechanism where Duloxetine's therapeutic effects on anxiety may contribute to its efficacy in treating MDD, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The overlapping indications across different pathways highlight a possible role of Duloxetine in modulating neural pathways associated with mood regulation, though further research is needed to establish a direct causal link.",
